    "updated_at": "2022-11-21T21:52:42Z",
    "body": "So unfortunately, I think I'm going to have to be that guy and say that I probably would vote to reject a change like the one currently proposed. Here's why:\r\n\r\nThis is proposing to add an extra config item to *every single runtime and language module*, which is only going to be used in a small fraction of cases, in order to mimic functionality that [we've already partially written](https://starship.rs/presets/plain-text.html). Will the `ascii_symbol` mirror the plaintext preset? If so, why have both? If not, where do they differ, and why? What if someone wants to add support for EBCDIC, do we need to add additional config options?\r\n\r\nI agree that the current preset-config system is not ideal for this due to the duplication issue, though I'm hopeful that this issue can be partially alleviated by #1887, and potentially even further by having a built-in preset system.\r\n\r\nI would be happy to see this addressed by a combination of #1887 and a change to the initscripts, or even better, by a fully-formed preset system (e.g. something which allows one to run `eval $(starship init --preset=ascii zsh)`), but adding 40+ configuration options just for the ability to run in tty is a very lopsided maintenance-burden-to-benefit-ratio.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
